{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-cancel-order","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"SQL injection vulnerability in order cancellation endpoint due to direct string formatting of the reason parameter into the SQL update statement.","category":"security","severity":"critical","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/orders.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":51,"end_line":52},"explanation":"The cancel_order endpoint interpolates `reason` directly into the SQL query string using an f-string (`f\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = '{reason}' WHERE id = ?\"`). This allows an attacker to inject arbitrary SQL statements via the `reason` JSON field. Parameterized queries should be used instead.","suggested_fix":"Use parameterized queries: `db.execute(\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = ? WHERE id = ?\", (reason, int(order_id)))`","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O4","note":"Reason string is directly formatted into the SQL query string rather than passed as a parameterized query argument.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/orders.py","start_line":51,"end_line":52,"snippet":"    sql = f\"UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled', cancel_reason = '{reason}' WHERE id = ?\"\n    db.execute(sql, (int(order_id),))","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O4","note":"db.execute receives the raw SQL string and order_id as a parameter, but cancel_reason is already interpolated via f-string.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/orders.py","start_line":52,"end_line":52,"snippet":"    db.execute(sql, (int(order_id),))","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"sqli","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":13678,"output_tokens":421,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":4,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":4,"tool_calls":3,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":5.941,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-inventory-set-role","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"set_role endpoint does not check if the user exists when updating their role or when notifying them, leading to 404 handling inconsistency and potential AttributeError when sending an email to a nonexistent user.","category":"correctness","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"app/routes/admin.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":33,"end_line":37},"explanation":"In `set_role`, unlike `deactivate_user`, there is no check to see if `db.execute` updated any rows. If a nonexistent `user_id` is supplied, the database update is a no-op and the endpoint proceeds. If `notify` is True, `get_user(db, int(user_id))` returns `None`, and accessing `user.email` raises an `AttributeError` (resulting in a 500 error instead of a 404). If `notify` is False, it returns 204 No Content even though no user was updated.","suggested_fix":"Check if the user exists or if db.execute modified any rows, and raise an HTTPError(404, \"user not found\") if not.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O2","note":"db.execute is called without checking if any rows were updated, and get_user can return None causing AttributeError on user.email if the user does not exist.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/admin.py","start_line":33,"end_line":37,"snippet":"    db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET role = ? WHERE id = ?\", (role, int(user_id)))\n    if not notify:\n        return Response(status=204)\n    user = get_user(db, int(user_id))\n    send_email(user.email, \"Your role has changed\", f\"You are now {role}.\")","query":null},{"role":"context","observation_id":"O10","note":"deactivate_user correctly checks if changed == 0 and raises a 404 HTTPError.","ref":"head","path":"app/routes/admin.py","start_line":20,"end_line":25,"snippet":"@router.post(\"/users/{user_id}/deactivate\")\ndef deactivate_user(request: Request, user_id: str) -> Response:\n    changed = db.execute(\"UPDATE users SET active = 0 WHERE id = ?\", (int(user_id),))\n    if changed == 0:\n        raise HTTPError(404, \"user not found\")\n    return Response(status=204)","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"none-user","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":2,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":30679,"output_tokens":1040,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":6018},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":7,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":7,"tool_calls":5,"rejections":1,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":80.127,"error":null}
