{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-number-converter-rename","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"The docstrings for IntegerConverter and FloatConverter still mention the old `signed` parameter instead of `allow_negative`.","category":"correctness","severity":"low","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":183,"end_line":184},"explanation":"The PR updates the code example in the docstrings for IntegerConverter and FloatConverter to use `allow_negative=True`, but the explanatory text above and below the example still refers to the parameter as `signed`.","suggested_fix":"Update the docstrings in IntegerConverter and FloatConverter to refer to `allow_negative` instead of `signed`.","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O30","note":"Docstring says The signed parameter will enable signed, negative values.","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","start_line":183,"end_line":184,"snippet":"    By default it only accepts unsigned, positive values. The ``signed``\n    parameter will enable signed, negative values. ::","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O32","note":"Docstring says The signed parameter will enable signed, negative values.","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/routing/converters.py","start_line":208,"end_line":209,"snippet":"    By default it only accepts unsigned, positive values. The ``signed``\n    parameter will enable signed, negative values. ::","query":null}]}],"matches":[],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":35553,"output_tokens":870,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":12125},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":6,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":6,"tool_calls":4,"rejections":1,"duplicates":0,"retries":2},"duration_seconds":87.234,"error":null}
{"case_id":"seeded-werkzeug-password-compare","kind":"seeded","sample":0,"findings":[{"id":"F1","title":"Replacing hmc.compare_digest with standard equality operator introduces timing attacks when comparing password hashes.","category":"security","severity":"high","confidence":"high","anchor":{"path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","side":"RIGHT","start_line":146,"end_line":146},"explanation":"Using `==` to compare password hashes leaks timing information about where the mismatch occurs, allowing an attacker to determine the hash byte-by-byte via timing side-channel attacks. `hmac.compare_digest` must be used for constant-time comparison of secret digests.","suggested_fix":"Restore hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)","anchor_in_diff":true,"evidence":[{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O1","note":"standard equality comparison is vulnerable to timing attacks","ref":"head","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return _hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0] == hashval","query":null},{"role":"defect_site","observation_id":"O2","note":"hmac.compare_digest was used previously to prevent timing attacks","ref":"base","path":"src/werkzeug/security.py","start_line":146,"end_line":146,"snippet":"    return hmac.compare_digest(_hash_internal(method, salt, password)[0], hashval)","query":null}]}],"matches":[{"finding_id":"F1","issue_id":"timing","distance":0,"verdict":"match","rationale":"location-only matching"}],"expected_total":1,"decoy_hits":[],"review_usage":{"input_tokens":10604,"output_tokens":377,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"judge_usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"thinking_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0},"cached":false,"requests":3,"cached_requests":0,"agent":{"suspects":0,"dropped_suspects":0,"outcomes":{},"stop_causes":{"submitted":1},"turns":3,"tool_calls":2,"rejections":0,"duplicates":0,"retries":0},"duration_seconds":26.79,"error":null}
